<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.1 LoRAct: Low-Rank Activation Compression ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that in the normal case the activation matrices are denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,…<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, while in the forward-compression case the corresponding activation matrices are denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>,…<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{N}^{{}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{N}^{{}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the given condition, we obtain <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="||{\bm{A}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Invoking the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="||f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1})-f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})||\leq L||{\bm{A}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq L\sigma_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1})-f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})||\leq L||{\bm{A}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq L\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In the normal case, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{2}=f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{2}=f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. While in the forward-compression case, we further compress <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="||{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}-f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})||\leq\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}-f_{1}({\bm{A}}_{1}^{{}^{\prime}})||\leq\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By the triangle inequality of the norm, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="||{\bm{A}}_{2}-{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq L\sigma_{1}+\sigma_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}_{2}-{\bm{A}}_{2}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq L\sigma_{1}+\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Proceeding in the same manner, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="||{\bm{A}}_{N}-{\bm{A}}_{N}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq\Sigma_{i=1}^{N}(L^{N-i}\sigma_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}_{N}-{\bm{A}}_{N}^{{}^{\prime}}||\leq\Sigma_{i=1}^{N}(L^{N-i}\sigma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Subsequently, the final activation is passed through the model’s linear layer, which is necessarily a Lipschitz continuous function. We assume its Lipschitz constant is denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{{\bm{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝑾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{{\bm{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, since the cross-entropy loss is globally Lipschitz continuous with respect to the logits, with Lipschitz constant <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we obtain the desired result:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(F({\bm{x}}),{\bm{y}})-\mathcal{L}(F_{comp}({\bm{x}}),{\bm{y}})\leq\sqrt{2}L_{{\bm{W}}}\Sigma_{i=1}^{N}(L^{N-i}\sigma_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝑾</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(F({\bm{x}}),{\bm{y}})-\mathcal{L}(F_{comp}({\bm{x}}),{\bm{y}})\leq\sqrt{2}L_{{\bm{W}}}\Sigma_{i=1}^{N}(L^{N-i}\sigma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Gaussian matrix, it is with high probability of full row rank. As our goal is to derive a lower bound for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math>, we may assume that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed of full row rank. In this case, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rank}({\bm{G}})=m-l=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rank}({\bm{G}})=m-l=k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\operatorname{Null}({\bm{G}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Null</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\operatorname{Null}({\bm{G}})</annotation></semantics></math> the null space of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(N)=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(N)=k</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the orthogonal projection onto <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}}){\bm{x}}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}}){\bm{x}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}+||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}})({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{N}){\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}+||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}})({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{N}){\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}=||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}-{\bm{I}}){\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}=||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since this inequality holds for all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may take the supremum over both sides to obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}})||\geq||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||(\frac{1}{l}{\bm{G}}^{T}{\bm{G}}{\bm{A}}-{\bm{A}})||\geq||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the first left singular vector, the first right singular vector, and the largest singular value of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||=\max_{||{\bm{x}}||=1}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||\geq||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{v}}_{1}||=||{\bm{P}}_{N}\sigma_{1}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=||{\bm{A}}||||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||=\max_{||{\bm{x}}||=1}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}||\geq||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}{\bm{v}}_{1}||=||{\bm{P}}_{N}\sigma_{1}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=||{\bm{A}}||||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||\geq\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=||{\bm{A}}||\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||\geq\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=||{\bm{A}}||\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||</annotation></semantics></math>. It thus remains to analyze <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Gaussian matrix independent of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is a uniformly random <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>
on the Grassmann manifold. For any fixed unit vector <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the random variable <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same distribution as the squared length obtained by projecting a uniformly distributed vector on the unit sphere <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> onto a random
<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace. A classical result states that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||^{2}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\frac{k}{2},\frac{m-k}{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||^{2}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\frac{k}{2},\frac{m-k}{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,
<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=\frac{\Gamma(\frac{k+1}{2})\Gamma(\frac{m}{2})}{\Gamma(\frac{k}{2})\Gamma(\frac{m+1}{2})}\geq\sqrt{\frac{m-l}{m+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{u}}_{1}||=\frac{\Gamma(\frac{k+1}{2})\Gamma(\frac{m}{2})}{\Gamma(\frac{k}{2})\Gamma(\frac{m+1}{2})}\geq\sqrt{\frac{m-l}{m+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. So <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||\geq\sqrt{\frac{m-l}{m+1}}\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{P}}_{N}{\bm{A}}||\geq\sqrt{\frac{m-l}{m+1}}\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, we have established the conclusion of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For ease of exposition, we first introduce some notation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{A}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{T}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&amp;\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}&{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\\
\bm{0}&amp;\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{V}}_{1}^{T}\\
{\bm{V}}_{2}^{T}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{A}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{T}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&amp;\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}&amp;{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\\
\bm{0}&amp;\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{V}}_{1}^{T}\\
{\bm{V}}_{2}^{T}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}={\bm{A}}\bm{\Omega}={\bm{Q}}{\bm{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑹</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}={\bm{A}}\bm{\Omega}={\bm{Q}}{\bm{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We denote that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}_{1}={\bm{V}}_{1}^{T}\bm{\Omega},\bm{\Omega}_{2}={\bm{V}}_{2}^{T}\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}_{1}={\bm{V}}_{1}^{T}\bm{\Omega},\bm{\Omega}_{2}={\bm{V}}_{2}^{T}\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}\begin{bmatrix}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
\bm{\Omega}_{2}\end{bmatrix}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{Y}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}\begin{bmatrix}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
\bm{\Omega}_{2}\end{bmatrix}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
We now begin the proof.
We denote that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{r}={\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{A}}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{V}}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{r}={\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{A}}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{V}}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Y}}_{r}={\bm{A}}_{r}\bm{\Omega}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Y}}_{r}={\bm{A}}_{r}\bm{\Omega}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then it can be derived</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}){\bm{A}}||=||{\bm{U}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}){\bm{U}}{\bm{A}}_{r}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}){\bm{A}}||=||{\bm{U}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}){\bm{U}}{\bm{A}}_{r}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents an orthogonal projection operator that satisfies <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{\bm{Y}})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Firstly, we consider the simpler condition where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>.
At this point, it is evident that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus we can observe:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{r}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1}\\
\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}\quad\text{and}\quad{\bm{Y}}_{r}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{r}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1}\\
\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}\quad\text{and}\quad{\bm{Y}}_{r}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}\\
\bm{0}\\
\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is of full row rank, it is evident that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{V}}_{1})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
That is <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})=\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projector onto <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{A}}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>, for any vector <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}{\bm{A}}_{r}{\bm{x}}={\bm{A}}_{r}{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}{\bm{A}}_{r}{\bm{x}}={\bm{A}}_{r}{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we conclude that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}{\bm{A}}_{r}={\bm{A}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}{\bm{A}}_{r}={\bm{A}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and thereby establish the conclusion of the theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">In the following, we address the more involved case where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>.
The idea of the proof is to reformulate <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a matrix with a more tractable structure, thereby facilitating a bound on <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}({\bm{A}})&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-rank full, and as a result, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}\bm{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is of full row rank. Thus, we can reformulate <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a block matrix, with one block being the identity matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,while the remaining part is considered as an interference term, which allows us to perform the scaling. Specifically: let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}={\bm{Y}}_{r}\cdot\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{-1}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}\\
{\bm{F}}\\
\mathbf{0}\end{bmatrix}\text{, where }{\bm{F}}={\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑰</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑭</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>, where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}={\bm{Y}}_{r}\cdot\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{-1}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}\\
{\bm{F}}\\
\mathbf{0}\end{bmatrix}\text{, where }{\bm{F}}={\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">It follows immediately that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Z}})\subseteq\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Z}})\subseteq\mathrm{Range}({\bm{Y}}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>,
Consequently, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}})\subseteq\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}})\subseteq\mathrm{Range}({\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, we derive the bound:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||\leq||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}_{r}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||\leq||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p">We know that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math> equals the largest singular value of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, also the square root of the largest eigenvalue of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can further bound it as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||^{2}=\lambda({\bm{A}}_{r}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}})^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r})=||{\bm{A}}_{r}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||^{2}=\lambda({\bm{A}}_{r}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}})^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r})=||{\bm{A}}_{r}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{A}}_{r}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p">The identities follow from the fact that an orthogonal projection operator is always idempotent, and the eigenvalues of a positive semi-definite matrix coincide with its singular values.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> has full column rank, it follows directly from the properties of orthogonal projection operators that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}={\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}^{T}{\bm{Z}})^{-1}{\bm{Z}}^{T}=\begin{bmatrix}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}F^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}={\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}^{T}{\bm{Z}})^{-1}{\bm{Z}}^{T}=\begin{bmatrix}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}F^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&{\bm{I}}-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&{\bm{I}}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>𝑰</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;{\bm{I}}-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&amp;{\bm{I}}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Halko et al. (2011)</a></cite>, for any positive semidefinite matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}\succeq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}\succeq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{M}})^{-1}\preceq{\bm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{M}})^{-1}\preceq{\bm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}\succeq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}\succeq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence, <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}\preceq{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}\preceq{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}\preceq{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}\preceq{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain the following strong conclusion:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}\preceq\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}&amp;-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&{\bm{I}}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&{\bm{I}}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>𝑰</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>𝑰</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}\preceq\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}&amp;-({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
-{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}&amp;{\bm{I}}&amp;\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathbf{0}&amp;{\bm{I}}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}\preceq\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&amp;-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\\
-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}^{2}\\
\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}\preceq\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&amp;-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\\
-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}&amp;{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}^{2}\\
\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2})^{T}=-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2})^{T}=-{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{F}}({\bm{I}}+{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}})^{-1}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
therefore, according to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Halko et al. (2011)</a></cite> we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}||\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}||+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}^{2}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}||^{2}=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒁</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑭</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Z}}}){\bm{\Sigma}}||\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{F}}^{T}{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}||+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}^{2}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{F}}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}||^{2}=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p">Combining the above arguments, we complete the proof. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our method is similar to RSVD in that it employs a sampling matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> to sample the row space of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
approximately capturing the top-<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> left singular vectors of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the result of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> plays a crucial role, motivating our effort to revise and present a corrected proof of it.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> states that when <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>𝟏</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> has full column rank, the approximation error admits a deterministic upper bound:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||^{2}\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||^{2}\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||^{2}+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By a simple relaxation we further obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||+||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the classical RSVD method, the sampling matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken to be a standard Gaussian matrix,
so <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely of full row rank, the upper bound for RSVD can be directly derived by invoking the conclusion of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and applying suitable relaxations based on the properties of standard Gaussian matrices.
However, in our method, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> relies on uniform random sampling from <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and thus <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not guaranteed to be of full row rank under all realizations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our proof strategy is to first analyze the quantities <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then define a favorable event accordingly.
This favorable event occurs with high probability and simultaneously satisfies Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, while its complement occurs with low probability.
We employ Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The Enhanced Decomposition Algorithm ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Memory-Efficient Fine-Tuning via Low-Rank Activation Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> to bound the expectation of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math> when restricted to the favorable event, and use probability arguments to control the expectation restricted to the complement of the favorable event. In this way, we obtain an upper bound on <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">First, we analyze the quantities <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the sampling matrix as <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{l\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{l\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}=({\bm{R}}{\bm{A}})^{T}={\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}=({\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}})^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}={\bm{V}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{S}}^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑹</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}=({\bm{R}}{\bm{A}})^{T}={\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}=({\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}})^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}={\bm{V}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{T}{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{S}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, according to the previous definitions, we have <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}=[{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}=[{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}=[\mathbf{0},{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}=[\mathbf{0},{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}[\mathbf{0},{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}([{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}[\mathbf{0},{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}([{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">In order to extract <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="([{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">([{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1},\mathbf{0}]{\bm{U}}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we reformulate <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{2}\bm{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}{\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||=||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the first <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> rows of <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}_{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}_{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th through <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th rows of <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By a simple rescaling, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||||({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}||||({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{1}^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma_{k+1}(A)}{\sigma_{k}(A)}||({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma_{k+1}(A)}{\sigma_{k}(A)}||({\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}({\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now define the good event. For any <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}(\epsilon)=\{\sigma_{min}({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T})\geq\sqrt{1-\epsilon}\land||{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}||\leq 1+\epsilon\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0em">∧</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}(\epsilon)=\{\sigma_{min}({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T})\geq\sqrt{1-\epsilon}\land||{\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T}||\leq 1+\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the notion of coherence: for an orthonormal matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>, its coherence is defined as
<math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{k}:=\frac{m}{k}\,\max_{1\leq i\leq m}||({\bm{U}}_{k})_{i,:}||_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}:=\frac{m}{k}\,\max_{1\leq i\leq m}||({\bm{U}}_{k})_{i,:}||_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">According to the classical matrix Chernoff–type results <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tropp et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen et al., 2020</a>)</cite>,
for every <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq C\frac{\mu_{k}k}{\epsilon^{2}}\log{\frac{k}{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq C\frac{\mu_{k}k}{\epsilon^{2}}\log{\frac{k}{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}(\epsilon))\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}(\epsilon))\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the subspace principal angle lemma and the conclusions of previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Magdon-Ismail, 2010</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen et al., 2016</a>)</cite>, we can further deduce that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||({\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||({\bm{U}}_{n-k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})({\bm{U}}_{k}^{T}{\bm{R}}^{T})^{+}||\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||\leq(C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}})\sigma_{k+1}({\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{\Sigma}}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{2}\mathbf{\Omega}_{1}^{+}||\leq(C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}})\sigma_{k+1}({\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||\leq(1+C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}})\sigma_{k+1}({\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||\leq(1+C\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}})\sigma_{k+1}({\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the expectation of <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math> when restricted to the favorable event.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we derive the expectation restricted to the complement of the favorable event. It is evident:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=\mathbb{E}||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}}){\bm{A}}||\leq\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||=||{\bm{A}}||\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}^{c})\leq\delta||{\bm{A}}||\leq ke^{\frac{-l\epsilon^{2}}{C\mu_{k}k}}||{\bm{A}}||." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||=\mathbb{E}||({\bm{I}}-{\bm{P}}_{{\bm{Y}}}){\bm{A}}||\leq\mathbb{E}||{\bm{A}}||=||{\bm{A}}||\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}^{c})\leq\delta||{\bm{A}}||\leq ke^{\frac{-l\epsilon^{2}}{C\mu_{k}k}}||{\bm{A}}||.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary positive real number, we may set <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{\mu_{k}k}{l}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this choice yields:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta||{\bm{A}}||\leq ke^{\frac{1}{C}}||{\bm{A}}||" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta||{\bm{A}}||\leq ke^{\frac{1}{C}}||{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.3" class="ltx_p">By adding the expectation of <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||{\bm{A}}-{\bm{Q}}{\bm{Q}}^{T}{\bm{A}}||</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to the favorable event and the expectation restricted to its complement, we obtain the desired conclusion. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Related Work</h3>

<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT) provides an effective strategy for adapting pre-trained models to downstream tasks. By modifying only a small subset of parameters, these methods achieve competitive performance compared with full fine-tuning.
The additive PEFT methods, like Adapter Tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Houlsby et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, Prompt Tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lester et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and Prefix Tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li &amp; Liang, 2021</a>)</cite>, keep the original model weights frozen and introduce new trainable components, but these approaches increase inference latency. Reparameterization-based PEFT methods, such as Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, operates by constraining trainable parameters within a low-rank subspace for each weight matrix. Besides, SPDF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Thangarasa et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, S<sup id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>FT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and SMT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite> leverage sparsity by selectively training only a subset of the model weights. However, a significant memory bottleneck still remains for existing PEFT methods, as these methods do not reduce the memory required for storing activations, thereby limiting their practicability in resource-constrained scenarios.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parameter Quantization and Decomposition</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The growing demand for computational efficiency highlights the deployment challenges posed by the large size of modern foundation models, particularly on edge devices.
Model quantization and decomposition serve as the principal strategies to mitigate this challenge. Existing quantization techniques generally fall into two categories: outlier-aware weight-only quantization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and joint activation-weight quantization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Regarding model decomposition, a straightforward application of SVD often harms performance, since weight matrices tend to be high-rank <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu &amp; Wu, 2023</a>)</cite>. To overcome this, FWSVD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hsu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, ASVD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and WeLore  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jaiswal et al., 2025</a>)</cite> decompose weights into low-rank matrices by preserving output similarity based on activations. LoSparse <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>)</cite> aim to recover high-rank information by additionally augmenting a low-rank component with a sparse matrix. The further approaches combine decomposition with quantization, representing weights as the sum of a low-rank component and a quantized matrix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Besides these inference-time optimizations, QLoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dettmers et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and LQ-LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2023</a>)</cite> reduce memory consumption for fine-tuning by first quantizing the pre-trained weights and then applying low-rank adaptation. However, the quantization and decomposition methods inevitably lead to a loss in model performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient and Optimizer State Compression</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce the memory consumption during training processes, recent work focuses on compressing gradients and optimizer states, considering they are naturally low-rank during training, which has been studied in both theory and practice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cosson et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Among existing approaches, GaLore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and FLoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> project gradients into a low-rank subspace for optimizer updates, thereby saving the memory cost. However, GaLore relies on SVD for constructing the projection matrix, which introduces non=negligible computational overhead. Moreover, the low-rank updating subspace is discontinuous. Subsequent research aims to mitigate these issues by improving the projection matrix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muhamed et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> or integrating GaLore with other optimizer-focused techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Different from the projection-based approaches, LoGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> uses a low-rank decomposition of weights specifically during the backward pass to compute activation gradients, thus accelerating the fine-tuning efficiency. Nevertheless, the memory consumed by activations is often neglected. This is especially pronounced under the PEFT setting, where activations become the primary memory bottleneck. Therefore, existing strategies focusing solely on gradients and optimizer states are unsuitable for PEFT.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Limitations and Discussions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While <span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LoRAct</span> demonstrates significant memory reduction and competitive performance across a wide range of tasks, its effectiveness is sensitive to the chosen compression ratio <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, under aggressive compression settings (e.g., <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;1/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;1/8</annotation></semantics></math> for vision tasks), a noticeable decline in accuracy is observed. This suggests that the activation compression may discard some critical information under certain fine-tuning scenarios. This limitation may pose challenges for <span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LoRAct</span> in some complex reasoning benchmarks, where the estimation errors may accumulate and then degrade model performance. Therefore, it is crucial to explore adaptive compression strategies with optimal <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> based on critical information, such as activation characteristics or task-specific requirements, and we leave this problem for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
